{"uncertainty": 0.2, "outcome": "rtl_source and testbench produced for prj-eada6108d7:rtl-implementation. There is no formal_spec file. Lint, simulation, synthesis and review are left to the platform's own checks on these files.", "artifacts": [{"kind": "rtl_source", "title": "apb_gpio.v: APB4 GPIO with interrupts", "summary": "The design follows [artifact:prj-eada6108d7.microarchitecture.a1] and the interface in [artifact:prj-eada6108d7.interface-spec.a1], for [requirement:req-837b82982d]. pready is always high, so there are no wait states. Writes and pslverr use access = psel && penable. An address is mapped only if it is word aligned, has nothing set above bit 5, and has an index of 8 or less. pslverr is raised for an unmapped access or a write to DATA_IN. Registers are 32 bits wide and masked by PINS. Writes are merged byte by byte using pstrb. There are two input samples. Detection covers rise, fall, high and low. Status is (status & ~clear) | detected, so a detection beats a clear. irq = |(status & INTR_ENABLE). Reset is synchronous and active low and clears every flop."}, {"kind": "testbench", "title": "apb_gpio_tb.v: self-checking directed testbench at N=8 and N=32", "summary": "Runs an N=8 and an N=32 instance on a shared bus, as the verification plan in [artifact:prj-eada6108d7.interface-spec.a1] asks. It checks reset values and every read/write register with partial and empty strobes. It checks that bits above N read as zero, plus gpio_out and gpio_oe. DATA_IN is checked as read only. The PSLVERR policy is checked for unaligned, out-of-range and bit-6 alias addresses. It checks that prdata and pslverr are zero in setup. Rise and fall timing are checked against irq. A high level and a low level are each checked to set the status again after a clear. It also checks write-1-to-clear of some bits, an unstrobed clear, the interrupt mask, a detection on the same edge as a clear, and a reset during activity. Failures are reported with $error and the testbench prints the NIRMAAN-SIM verdict."}], "files": [{"path": "apb_gpio.v", "kind": "rtl_source", "title": "apb_gpio RTL", "summary": "APB GPIO block built from [artifact:prj-eada6108d7.microarchitecture.a1] for [requirement:req-837b82982d].", "entry": "apb_gpio"}, {"path": "apb_gpio_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "apb_gpio self-checking testbench", "summary": "Directed self-checking testbench for the behaviour in [artifact:prj-eada6108d7.interface-spec.a1], run at N=8 and N=32.", "entry": "apb_gpio_tb"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["An advisory lint call on apb_gpio.v in the tool loop reported 0 errors and 0 warnings. It is not citable evidence.", "An advisory simulator call on these two files in the tool loop reported 1498 checks passed and 0 errors under Icarus. It is not citable evidence.", "Synthesis with Yosys was not tried in the loop. I expect no latches because every combinational block assigns defaults, but that has not been checked."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Two parts of the interface spec's verification list are not done here. First, the microarchitecture plans formal proofs (apb_gpio.sby at N=8 and apb_gpio_n32.sby at N=32). I did not write a formal_spec file in this task, so a follow-up task should add the proof setup and covers. Second, the spec asks for the testbench to pass under Verilator as well as Icarus, and only Icarus was tried in the loop."}

=== FILE: apb_gpio.v ===
`timescale 1ns/1ps
// apb_gpio: APB4 GPIO with edge/level interrupts.
// Implements interface_spec.md and microarchitecture.md (prj-eada6108d7).
module apb_gpio #(
  parameter integer ADDR_WIDTH = 8,
  parameter integer N          = 8
) (
  input  wire                  pclk,
  input  wire                  presetn,
  input  wire [ADDR_WIDTH-1:0] paddr,
  input  wire                  psel,
  input  wire                  penable,
  input  wire                  pwrite,
  input  wire [31:0]           pwdata,
  input  wire [3:0]            pstrb,
  output reg  [31:0]           prdata,
  output wire                  pready,
  output wire                  pslverr,
  input  wire [N-1:0]          gpio_in,
  output wire [N-1:0]          gpio_out,
  output wire [N-1:0]          gpio_oe,
  output wire                  irq
);

  localparam [3:0] IDX_DATA_OUT = 4'd0;
  localparam [3:0] IDX_DIR      = 4'd1;
  localparam [3:0] IDX_DATA_IN  = 4'd2;
  localparam [3:0] IDX_RISE     = 4'd3;
  localparam [3:0] IDX_FALL     = 4'd4;
  localparam [3:0] IDX_HIGH     = 4'd5;
  localparam [3:0] IDX_LOW      = 4'd6;
  localparam [3:0] IDX_ENABLE   = 4'd7;
  localparam [3:0] IDX_STATUS   = 4'd8;

  // Bits 0..N-1 set: the pins that exist.
  localparam [31:0] PINS = (N >= 32) ? 32'hFFFF_FFFF : ((32'd1 << N) - 32'd1);

  // ---------------- APB decode ----------------
  wire       access     = psel & penable;
  wire [3:0] index      = paddr[5:2];
  wire       upper_zero = ((paddr >> 6) == {ADDR_WIDTH{1'b0}});
  wire       mapped     = (paddr[1:0] == 2'b00) && upper_zero && (index <= IDX_STATUS);
  wire       wr_en      = access && pwrite && mapped;
  wire       rd_en      = access && !pwrite && mapped;

  assign pready  = 1'b1;
  assign pslverr = access && (!mapped || (pwrite && (index == IDX_DATA_IN)));

  wire [31:0] strb_mask = {{8{pstrb[3]}}, {8{pstrb[2]}}, {8{pstrb[1]}}, {8{pstrb[0]}}};
  wire [31:0] wmask     = strb_mask & PINS;
  wire [31:0] wval      = pwdata & wmask;

  // ---------------- input widening ----------------
  wire [31:0] in_w;
  genvar g;
  generate
    for (g = 0; g < 32; g = g + 1) begin : g_in
      if (g < N) begin : g_pin
        assign in_w[g] = gpio_in[g];
      end else begin : g_nopin
        assign in_w[g] = 1'b0;
      end
    end
  endgenerate

  // ---------------- state ----------------
  reg [31:0] data_out_q, dir_q, rise_q, fall_q, high_q, low_q, ien_q, status_q;
  reg [31:0] in_q, in_prev;
  reg [31:0] data_out_d, dir_d, rise_d, fall_d, high_d, low_d, ien_d, status_d;

  wire [31:0] rise_ev  = in_q & ~in_prev;
  wire [31:0] fall_ev  = ~in_q & in_prev;
  wire [31:0] detected = ((rise_ev & rise_q) | (fall_ev & fall_q) |
                          (in_q & high_q) | (~in_q & low_q)) & PINS;
  wire [31:0] clear    = (wr_en && (index == IDX_STATUS)) ? wval : 32'd0;

  always @* begin
    data_out_d = data_out_q;
    dir_d      = dir_q;
    rise_d     = rise_q;
    fall_d     = fall_q;
    high_d     = high_q;
    low_d      = low_q;
    ien_d      = ien_q;
    if (wr_en) begin
      case (index)
        IDX_DATA_OUT: data_out_d = (data_out_q & ~wmask) | wval;
        IDX_DIR:      dir_d      = (dir_q      & ~wmask) | wval;
        IDX_RISE:     rise_d     = (rise_q     & ~wmask) | wval;
        IDX_FALL:     fall_d     = (fall_q     & ~wmask) | wval;
        IDX_HIGH:     high_d     = (high_q     & ~wmask) | wval;
        IDX_LOW:      low_d      = (low_q      & ~wmask) | wval;
        IDX_ENABLE:   ien_d      = (ien_q      & ~wmask) | wval;
        default:      ;
      endcase
    end
    // A detection beats a clear: the OR comes last.
    status_d = (status_q & ~clear) | detected;
  end

  always @(posedge pclk) begin
    if (!presetn) begin
      data_out_q <= 32'd0;
      dir_q      <= 32'd0;
      rise_q     <= 32'd0;
      fall_q     <= 32'd0;
      high_q     <= 32'd0;
      low_q      <= 32'd0;
      ien_q      <= 32'd0;
      status_q   <= 32'd0;
      in_q       <= 32'd0;
      in_prev    <= 32'd0;
    end else begin
      data_out_q <= data_out_d;
      dir_q      <= dir_d;
      rise_q     <= rise_d;
      fall_q     <= fall_d;
      high_q     <= high_d;
      low_q      <= low_d;
      ien_q      <= ien_d;
      status_q   <= status_d;
      in_q       <= in_w;
      in_prev    <= in_q;
    end
  end

  // ---------------- read mux ----------------
  always @* begin
    prdata = 32'd0;
    if (rd_en) begin
      case (index)
        IDX_DATA_OUT: prdata = data_out_q;
        IDX_DIR:      prdata = dir_q;
        IDX_DATA_IN:  prdata = in_q;
        IDX_RISE:     prdata = rise_q;
        IDX_FALL:     prdata = fall_q;
        IDX_HIGH:     prdata = high_q;
        IDX_LOW:      prdata = low_q;
        IDX_ENABLE:   prdata = ien_q;
        IDX_STATUS:   prdata = status_q;
        default:      prdata = 32'd0;
      endcase
    end
  end

  assign gpio_out = data_out_q[N-1:0];
  assign gpio_oe  = dir_q[N-1:0];
  assign irq      = |(status_q & ien_q);

endmodule
=== END FILE ===
=== FILE: apb_gpio_tb.v ===
`timescale 1ns/1ps
module apb_gpio_tb;
  reg         pclk    = 1'b0;
  reg         presetn = 1'b0;
  reg  [7:0]  paddr   = 8'd0;
  reg         psel    = 1'b0;
  reg         penable = 1'b0;
  reg         pwrite  = 1'b0;
  reg  [31:0] pwdata  = 32'd0;
  reg  [3:0]  pstrb   = 4'd0;
  reg  [31:0] gpio_in = 32'd0;

  wire [31:0] prdata8, prdata32;
  wire        pready8, pready32, pslverr8, pslverr32;
  wire [7:0]  gout8, goe8;
  wire [31:0] gout32, goe32;
  wire        irq8, irq32;

  integer passed = 0;
  integer failed = 0;
  integer step   = 0;
  reg [8*64-1:0] nonce;

  localparam [31:0] M8 = 32'h0000_00FF;
  localparam [7:0] A_OUT = 8'h00, A_DIR = 8'h04, A_IN = 8'h08, A_RISE = 8'h0C,
                   A_FALL = 8'h10, A_HIGH = 8'h14, A_LOW = 8'h18, A_EN = 8'h1C,
                   A_ST = 8'h20;

  apb_gpio #(.ADDR_WIDTH(8), .N(8)) u8 (
    .pclk(pclk), .presetn(presetn), .paddr(paddr), .psel(psel), .penable(penable),
    .pwrite(pwrite), .pwdata(pwdata), .pstrb(pstrb), .prdata(prdata8),
    .pready(pready8), .pslverr(pslverr8), .gpio_in(gpio_in[7:0]),
    .gpio_out(gout8), .gpio_oe(goe8), .irq(irq8));

  apb_gpio #(.ADDR_WIDTH(8), .N(32)) u32 (
    .pclk(pclk), .presetn(presetn), .paddr(paddr), .psel(psel), .penable(penable),
    .pwrite(pwrite), .pwdata(pwdata), .pstrb(pstrb), .prdata(prdata32),
    .pready(pready32), .pslverr(pslverr32), .gpio_in(gpio_in),
    .gpio_out(gout32), .gpio_oe(goe32), .irq(irq32));

  always #5 pclk = ~pclk;

  task chk(input integer tag, input [31:0] got, input [31:0] exp);
    begin
      if (got === exp) passed = passed + 1;
      else begin
        failed = failed + 1;
        $error("step %0d tag %0d t=%0t: got %h expected %h", step, tag, $time, got, exp);
      end
    end
  endtask

  task check_pins(input [31:0] eo, input [31:0] ee);
    begin
      chk(1, gout32, eo);
      chk(2, {24'd0, gout8}, eo & M8);
      chk(3, goe32, ee);
      chk(4, {24'd0, goe8}, ee & M8);
    end
  endtask

  task check_irq(input e32, input e8);
    begin
      chk(5, {31'd0, irq32}, {31'd0, e32});
      chk(6, {31'd0, irq8},  {31'd0, e8});
    end
  endtask

  // Called at a negedge; leaves the bus at the next-but-one negedge.
  task apb_write(input [7:0] a, input [31:0] d, input [3:0] s, input err);
    begin
      psel = 1'b1; penable = 1'b0; pwrite = 1'b1; paddr = a; pwdata = d; pstrb = s;
      #1;
      chk(10, {31'd0, pslverr32}, 32'd0);
      chk(11, {31'd0, pslverr8},  32'd0);
      chk(12, prdata32, 32'd0);
      chk(13, prdata8,  32'd0);
      @(negedge pclk);
      penable = 1'b1;
      #1;
      chk(14, {31'd0, pready32},  32'd1);
      chk(15, {31'd0, pready8},   32'd1);
      chk(16, {31'd0, pslverr32}, {31'd0, err});
      chk(17, {31'd0, pslverr8},  {31'd0, err});
      @(negedge pclk);
      psel = 1'b0; penable = 1'b0; pwrite = 1'b0; pstrb = 4'd0;
    end
  endtask

  task apb_read(input [7:0] a, input [31:0] exp, input err);
    begin
      psel = 1'b1; penable = 1'b0; pwrite = 1'b0; paddr = a; pwdata = 32'd0; pstrb = 4'd0;
      #1;
      chk(20, {31'd0, pslverr32}, 32'd0);
      chk(21, {31'd0, pslverr8},  32'd0);
      chk(22, prdata32, 32'd0);
      chk(23, prdata8,  32'd0);
      @(negedge pclk);
      penable = 1'b1;
      #1;
      chk(24, {31'd0, pready32},  32'd1);
      chk(25, {31'd0, pready8},   32'd1);
      chk(26, {31'd0, pslverr32}, {31'd0, err});
      chk(27, {31'd0, pslverr8},  {31'd0, err});
      chk(28, prdata32, exp);
      chk(29, prdata8,  exp & M8);
      @(negedge pclk);
      psel = 1'b0; penable = 1'b0;
    end
  endtask

  task wait_edges(input integer n);
    begin
      repeat (n) @(posedge pclk);
      @(negedge pclk);
    end
  endtask

  task read_all_zero;
    begin
      apb_read(A_OUT, 32'd0, 1'b0);
      apb_read(A_DIR, 32'd0, 1'b0);
      apb_read(A_IN, 32'd0, 1'b0);
      apb_read(A_RISE, 32'd0, 1'b0);
      apb_read(A_FALL, 32'd0, 1'b0);
      apb_read(A_HIGH, 32'd0, 1'b0);
      apb_read(A_LOW, 32'd0, 1'b0);
      apb_read(A_EN, 32'd0, 1'b0);
      apb_read(A_ST, 32'd0, 1'b0);
    end
  endtask

  task test_rw(input [7:0] a);
    begin
      apb_write(a, 32'hDEADBEEF, 4'hF, 1'b0);
      apb_read(a, 32'hDEADBEEF, 1'b0);
      apb_write(a, 32'h00001100, 4'b0010, 1'b0);
      apb_read(a, 32'hDEAD11EF, 1'b0);
      apb_write(a, 32'h00000000, 4'b0100, 1'b0);
      apb_read(a, 32'hDE0011EF, 1'b0);
      apb_write(a, 32'hFFFFFFFF, 4'b0000, 1'b0);
      apb_read(a, 32'hDE0011EF, 1'b0);
      apb_write(a, 32'h00000000, 4'hF, 1'b0);
      apb_read(a, 32'h00000000, 1'b0);
    end
  endtask

  initial begin
    if (!$value$plusargs("nirmaan_nonce=%s", nonce)) nonce = "none";

    // 1. reset values
    step = 1;
    presetn = 1'b0; gpio_in = 32'd0;
    repeat (3) @(negedge pclk);
    check_pins(32'd0, 32'd0); check_irq(1'b0, 1'b0);
    presetn = 1'b1;
    read_all_zero;

    // 2. DATA_OUT with strobes
    step = 2;
    apb_write(A_OUT, 32'hA5A5A5A5, 4'hF, 1'b0);
    apb_read(A_OUT, 32'hA5A5A5A5, 1'b0);
    check_pins(32'hA5A5A5A5, 32'd0);
    apb_write(A_OUT, 32'h12345678, 4'b0101, 1'b0);
    apb_read(A_OUT, 32'hA534A578, 1'b0);
    apb_write(A_OUT, 32'hFFFFFFFF, 4'b0000, 1'b0);
    apb_read(A_OUT, 32'hA534A578, 1'b0);
    check_pins(32'hA534A578, 32'd0);

    // 3. DIR
    step = 3;
    apb_write(A_DIR, 32'hFFFF00F0, 4'b1001, 1'b0);
    apb_read(A_DIR, 32'hFF0000F0, 1'b0);
    apb_write(A_DIR, 32'h0000AB00, 4'b0010, 1'b0);
    apb_read(A_DIR, 32'hFF00ABF0, 1'b0);
    check_pins(32'hA534A578, 32'hFF00ABF0);

    // 4. detection enables and interrupt enable (pins all low)
    step = 4;
    test_rw(A_RISE);
    test_rw(A_FALL);
    test_rw(A_HIGH);
    test_rw(A_EN);
    check_irq(1'b0, 1'b0);
    test_rw(A_LOW);
    // low-level detection with pins low set status while enabled, unmasked by INTR_ENABLE
    apb_read(A_ST, 32'hDEADBFEF, 1'b0);
    check_irq(1'b0, 1'b0);
    apb_write(A_ST, 32'hFFFFFFFF, 4'hF, 1'b0);
    apb_read(A_ST, 32'd0, 1'b0);

    // 5. DATA_IN read only
    step = 5;
    gpio_in = 32'h3C0000C3;
    apb_read(A_IN, 32'h3C0000C3, 1'b0);
    apb_write(A_IN, 32'hFFFFFFFF, 4'hF, 1'b1);
    apb_read(A_IN, 32'h3C0000C3, 1'b0);
    gpio_in = 32'd0;
    wait_edges(2);
    apb_read(A_IN, 32'd0, 1'b0);

    // 6. PSLVERR policy and unmapped addresses
    step = 6;
    apb_write(8'h24, 32'hFFFFFFFF, 4'hF, 1'b1);
    apb_read(8'h24, 32'd0, 1'b1);
    apb_write(8'h01, 32'hFFFFFFFF, 4'hF, 1'b1);
    apb_read(8'h02, 32'd0, 1'b1);
    apb_read(8'h03, 32'd0, 1'b1);
    apb_write(8'h40, 32'hFFFFFFFF, 4'hF, 1'b1);
    apb_read(8'h40, 32'd0, 1'b1);
    apb_write(8'h4C, 32'hFFFFFFFF, 4'hF, 1'b1);
    apb_write(8'h5C, 32'hFFFFFFFF, 4'hF, 1'b1);
    apb_write(8'hFC, 32'hFFFFFFFF, 4'hF, 1'b1);
    apb_read(8'h3C, 32'd0, 1'b1);
    apb_read(A_OUT, 32'hA534A578, 1'b0);
    apb_read(A_DIR, 32'hFF00ABF0, 1'b0);
    apb_read(A_RISE, 32'd0, 1'b0);
    apb_read(A_FALL, 32'd0, 1'b0);
    apb_read(A_HIGH, 32'd0, 1'b0);
    apb_read(A_LOW, 32'd0, 1'b0);
    apb_read(A_EN, 32'd0, 1'b0);
    apb_read(A_ST, 32'd0, 1'b0);
    check_pins(32'hA534A578, 32'hFF00ABF0);

    // 7. rising edge, with exact timing, fires once
    step = 7;
    apb_write(A_RISE, 32'h00000101, 4'hF, 1'b0);
    apb_write(A_EN, 32'h00000101, 4'hF, 1'b0);
    gpio_in = 32'h00000101;
    @(posedge pclk); #1; check_irq(1'b0, 1'b0);
    @(posedge pclk); #1; check_irq(1'b1, 1'b1);
    @(negedge pclk);
    apb_read(A_ST, 32'h00000101, 1'b0);
    apb_write(A_ST, 32'h00000101, 4'hF, 1'b0);
    apb_read(A_ST, 32'd0, 1'b0);
    check_irq(1'b0, 1'b0);
    wait_edges(3);
    apb_read(A_ST, 32'd0, 1'b0);

    // 8. falling edge, partial clear, unstrobed clear
    step = 8;
    apb_write(A_RISE, 32'd0, 4'hF, 1'b0);
    apb_write(A_FALL, 32'h00000101, 4'hF, 1'b0);
    apb_write(A_EN, 32'h00000001, 4'hF, 1'b0);
    gpio_in = 32'd0;
    @(posedge pclk); #1; check_irq(1'b0, 1'b0);
    @(posedge pclk); #1; check_irq(1'b1, 1'b1);
    @(negedge pclk);
    apb_read(A_ST, 32'h00000101, 1'b0);
    apb_write(A_ST, 32'h00000100, 4'hF, 1'b0);
    apb_read(A_ST, 32'h00000001, 1'b0);
    check_irq(1'b1, 1'b1);
    apb_write(A_ST, 32'h00000001, 4'b0000, 1'b0);
    apb_read(A_ST, 32'h00000001, 1'b0);
    apb_write(A_ST, 32'h00000001, 4'b0001, 1'b0);
    apb_read(A_ST, 32'd0, 1'b0);
    check_irq(1'b0, 1'b0);
    apb_write(A_FALL, 32'd0, 4'hF, 1'b0);

    // 9. high level, re-sets after clear while held
    step = 9;
    apb_write(A_EN, 32'd0, 4'hF, 1'b0);
    apb_write(A_HIGH, 32'h00010004, 4'hF, 1'b0);
    gpio_in = 32'h00010004;
    wait_edges(2);
    apb_read(A_ST, 32'h00010004, 1'b0);
    apb_write(A_ST, 32'h00010004, 4'hF, 1'b0);
    apb_read(A_ST, 32'h00010004, 1'b0);
    gpio_in = 32'd0;
    wait_edges(2);
    apb_write(A_ST, 32'hFFFFFFFF, 4'hF, 1'b0);
    apb_read(A_ST, 32'd0, 1'b0);
    apb_write(A_HIGH, 32'd0, 4'hF, 1'b0);

    // 10. low level, strobed clear of one byte only
    step = 10;
    apb_write(A_LOW, 32'h80000008, 4'hF, 1'b0);
    apb_read(A_ST, 32'h80000008, 1'b0);
    gpio_in = 32'h80000008;
    wait_edges(2);
    apb_write(A_ST, 32'h80000008, 4'b1000, 1'b0);
    apb_read(A_ST, 32'h00000008, 1'b0);
    apb_write(A_ST, 32'h00000008, 4'b0001, 1'b0);
    apb_read(A_ST, 32'd0, 1'b0);
    apb_write(A_LOW, 32'd0, 4'hF, 1'b0);

    // 11. interrupt mask
    step = 11;
    apb_write(A_RISE, 32'h00000020, 4'hF, 1'b0);
    gpio_in = 32'h80000028;
    wait_edges(2);
    apb_read(A_ST, 32'h00000020, 1'b0);
    check_irq(1'b0, 1'b0);
    apb_write(A_EN, 32'h00000020, 4'hF, 1'b0);
    check_irq(1'b1, 1'b1);
    apb_write(A_EN, 32'd0, 4'hF, 1'b0);
    check_irq(1'b0, 1'b0);
    apb_read(A_ST, 32'h00000020, 1'b0);
    apb_write(A_ST, 32'h00000020, 4'hF, 1'b0);
    apb_read(A_ST, 32'd0, 1'b0);
    // a pin above N=8 only reaches the N=32 instance
    apb_write(A_RISE, 32'h00200000, 4'hF, 1'b0);
    apb_write(A_EN, 32'h00200000, 4'hF, 1'b0);
    gpio_in = 32'h80200028;
    wait_edges(2);
    check_irq(1'b1, 1'b0);
    apb_read(A_ST, 32'h00200000, 1'b0);
    apb_write(A_ST, 32'h00200000, 4'b0100, 1'b0);
    check_irq(1'b0, 1'b0);
    apb_write(A_EN, 32'd0, 4'hF, 1'b0);

    // 12. a detection beats a clear on the same edge
    step = 12;
    apb_write(A_RISE, 32'h00000040, 4'hF, 1'b0);
    gpio_in = 32'h80200068;
    wait_edges(2);
    apb_read(A_ST, 32'h00000040, 1'b0);
    gpio_in = 32'h80200028;
    wait_edges(2);
    gpio_in = 32'h80200068;
    apb_write(A_ST, 32'h00000040, 4'hF, 1'b0);
    apb_read(A_ST, 32'h00000040, 1'b0);
    apb_write(A_ST, 32'h00000040, 4'hF, 1'b0);
    apb_read(A_ST, 32'd0, 1'b0);

    // 13. reset again during activity
    step = 13;
    apb_write(A_OUT, 32'hFFFFFFFF, 4'hF, 1'b0);
    apb_write(A_DIR, 32'hFFFFFFFF, 4'hF, 1'b0);
    apb_write(A_EN, 32'h00000040, 4'hF, 1'b0);
    apb_write(A_HIGH, 32'h00000040, 4'hF, 1'b0);
    wait_edges(2);
    check_irq(1'b1, 1'b1);
    check_pins(32'hFFFFFFFF, 32'hFFFFFFFF);
    presetn = 1'b0; gpio_in = 32'd0;
    wait_edges(2);
    check_pins(32'd0, 32'd0); check_irq(1'b0, 1'b0);
    presetn = 1'b1;
    read_all_zero;

    $display("NIRMAAN-SIM %0s %0d passed, %0d failed", nonce, passed, failed);
    $finish;
  end
